Two serious contradictions are now confirmed.

First, a “disposable working copy” is not automatically isolated: the working copies used here share the same underlying Git storage and branch records. An agent can corrupt or rewrite shared project history even if its visible folder is disposable.

Second, the proposed “tiny release service” is not the only trusted piece. The document gives the much larger harness the same trusted identity and lets it write approvals and verdicts. If that harness is fooled or compromised, it can manufacture the facts the release service relies on.
